PAOFLOW examples

Every example is a case: ./cases/<name>/

- One folder per calculation: its inputs (Quantum ESPRESSO, VASP or a model Hamiltonian), a
  README.md and case.json. The pseudopotentials live once in ../PSEUDOS (mostly ../PSEUDOS/library)
  and are copied in with the case.
- PAOFLOW Studio: Setup tab, "Examples...", pick a case and a folder: Studio copies it and lists
  its runs in the Runs tab. Command line: `paoflow-gen --example <name>` (`paoflow-gen --example
  list` shows the cases).
- Two kinds of case. A *generator* case gives the workflow of paoflow-gen and the answers of its
  form: Studio fills the form, and the drivers (main.py, plot.py) are written from it. A *scripts*
  case brings its own drivers (models, analyses, multi-stage folders, recipes): Studio opens Runs
  on its steps, with no form.
- The reference outputs of the generator cases are in the integration-test tarballs (the releases
  tagged integration-assets-*), not in the repository.

Generator cases

- Property runs: si_bands_transport, al_dos_transport, pt_spin_polarized (nspin = 2),
  fe_anomalous_hall, pt_spin_hall, alp_hubbard_optics (Hubbard shifts + dielectric tensor),
  pt_adhoc_soc (ad hoc spin-orbit), snte_spin_texture (2D), mop2_weyl_points,
  gaas_doped_transport (doping and scattering models), te_rashba_edelstein,
  bi_ribbon_edge_states (site-projected bands), bi_bilayer_z2 (Z2 invariant), pt_slab_layer_shc
  (layer-resolved spin Hall), si_optics (dielectric function, JDOS), snte_mirror_chern,
  pd_spin_susceptibility.
- Landauer transport: al_bulk_landauer, alh_junction_landauer (eigenchannels).
- ACBN0 / eACBN0: gaas_acbn0, mgo_acbn0, mno_acbn0 (antiferromagnetic), si_acbn0, zno_acbn0.
- These cases use PAOFLOW's internal projections on the bases generated from their
  pseudopotentials; projwfc.x stays an option in the form (Studio then writes proj.in and adds the
  projwfc.x run).

Scripts cases

- Electron-phonon system folders (system.py, qe/, phonons/, coupling/, superconductivity/,
  optics/, transport/, arpes/; the layout `paoflow-gen elphon` writes): si_elphon
  (phonon-assisted absorption, emissivity, mobility, ARPES), pb_elphon (Eliashberg function, Tc,
  Migdal-Eliashberg gap, resistivity, infrared optics, ARPES kink, special displacements),
  mgb2_elphon (anisotropic two-gap Migdal-Eliashberg), sic_elphon (polar crystal: Frohlich
  coupling, quadrupoles, mobility).
- Non-linear optics: gaas_nlo (PAW GaAs, with REPORT.md: the comparison with the literature),
  ges_nlo (monolayer GeS), graphene_nlo_model, kane_mele_nlo_model, mos2_nlo_model (shift and
  injection currents, second-harmonic generation).
- Tight-binding models run through PAOFLOW(model=...): graphene_tb_model (with the list of the
  model labels), graphene_berry_phase_model, cubium_tb_model, kane_mele_tb_model,
  si_slater_koster_model. The model runs of paoflow-gen / Studio (workflow tb_model) cover the
  built-in models.
- Band unfolding: si_supercell_unfold, tbg_unfold (twisted bilayer graphene, dense and sparse).
- Quantum oscillations: bi_pyskeaf (extremal orbits with pyskeaf), nbsn2_qo_analysis (computed
  frequencies against measured quantum oscillations).
- VASP: vasp_overview (the notebook of all seven systems) and vasp_si_bands, vasp_pt_spin_hall,
  vasp_fe_anomalous_hall, vasp_mnf2_afm_bands, vasp_mn3ir_noncollinear_bands, vasp_ferh_bands,
  vasp_cri3_monolayer_bands.
- Basis presets on norm-conserving and ultrasoft, scalar and fully relativistic pseudopotentials:
  si_oncv_basis_presets, si_uspp_basis_presets, pt_oncv_basis_presets, pt_uspp_basis_presets.
- Sparse backend on a doubled cell: si_sparse_backend.
- Low-level Transport calls of a conductor with a defect: al_transport_defect.

The Results and Plots tabs of paoflow-studio show the outputs of any case. clean_runs.py removes
the outputs of runs made in place, keeping inputs, data and references.
